tention, but communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education. B reliability, stress, technical competence, but pretentious, wrong tone, no crew cooperation evidence. D responsibility, problem solving, but arrogance, weak leadership. A unknown.\n\nWe need to decide. Perhaps we can shift to B, aligning with majority, but we need to justify. Or we could maintain C, but need to address concerns. The panel is split 2-1 for B vs C. We can argue that B's strengths outweigh C's concerns, and lack of crew cooperation evidence for B is a gap but not a disqualifier. Also C's egocentric and unwillingness to further education may be more serious for long-term development. So we can change vote to B.\n\nThus we will produce public message: I agree with B, explain why, referencing facts: very conscientious, handles stress, good weather assessment, computer skills, and note that communication issues are less severe than C's egocentric and lack of adaptability. Also note D's temperament issues. Then vote for Candidate B.\n\nOutput format: PUBLIC_MESSAGE then METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate B.\n\nProceed."}
